# Normalize all text files to LF
* text=auto eol=lf

# Unity specific files
*.cs text eol=lf
*.shader text eol=lf
*.cginc text eol=lf

*.meta text eol=lf

# .unity / .prefab / .asset are DELIBERATELY not forced to text. Unity writes some
# of them as binary regardless of ForceText serialization (terrain heightmaps, baked
# NavMesh and lighting data, and any scene saved before ForceText was enabled).
# Forcing `text` on those extensions overrides git's own binary detection, so the
# clean filter strips every 0x0D byte that happens to precede a 0x0A inside the
# payload — silently, a few bytes per commit, until Unity reports
# "Unknown error occurred while loading <asset>". The `* text=auto eol=lf` rule at
# the top already normalizes the YAML ones to LF while leaving real binaries alone;
# do not add `*.asset text` / `*.unity text` / `*.prefab text` rules back.
#
# Belt-and-braces for the families that are always binary, matched by filename so
# they stay protected when the project is restructured (an earlier version of this
# file pinned full paths, and moving Assets/Terrain -> Assets/Game/Terrain silently
# unprotected all of them):
TerrainData*.asset binary
*[Tt]errain*.asset binary
*NavMesh*.asset binary
LightingData.asset binary
ReflectionProbe*.exr binary
Lightmap*.exr binary

# ...but ProjectSettings/*.asset is always YAML, so keep NavMeshAreas.asset diffable.
ProjectSettings/*.asset text eol=lf

# JSON / config
*.json text eol=lf
*.xml text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf

# Binary files (do not touch line endings)
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.fbx binary
*.mp4 binary
